{
  "slug": "sindri",
  "name": "Sindri",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Sindri turns a one-line goal like \"reduce bundle_bytes by 15%\" into an autonomous, overnight experiment loop. It proposes candidates,applies them in fresh subagent contexts, runs your benchmark, keeps the wins as git commits, reverts the losses, and opens a PR with a human-readable log. One commit per kept experiment. Git is the audit log.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills** and **8 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `sindri-finalize` (Auto-invoked by sindri-loop on clean termination with ≥1 kept commit), `sindri-loop` (The sindri orchestrator), `sindri-scaffold-benchmark` (Scaffold .claude/scripts/sindri/benchmark.py by scanning the repo, proposing a measurement in natural language, translating the user's refinements into Python,…), `sindri-start` (Interactive, one-shot scaffolding for a new sindri optimization run)\n- **Commands** (8): `clear` (Abandon the current sindri run — destructive; deletes run state and the run branch), `finalize` (ADVANCED/DEBUG), `forge` (Start a new sindri optimization run from a goal statement — bounded, target-driven experiments on any deterministic metric), `help` (Show the sindri command list and a one-line overview of each), `loop` (ADVANCED/DEBUG), `setup` (Scaffold or repair the benchmark script for a sindri run), `status` (Print the status of the current sindri run (or report that there is no active run)), `stop` (Signal the current sindri run to halt at its next wakeup)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sindri@claude-community` from `4KMetrics/sindri`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
